## YAAP
- [OpenAI Banned Me for Building This](https://www.ai21.com/yaap/openai-banned-me-for-building-this/): MCP wasn't enough, so Corey J\. Gallon wired his agent straight into Chrome\. It could share his browser session, beat CAPTCHAs, even take over mid\-task\. Then OpenAI tried to ban him for it\. Yuval gets the full story: CDP, scraping, outreach automation, and how he talked his way out of the ban\.
- [Your Code Doesn't Need to Be Readable Anymore](https://www.ai21.com/yaap/your-code-doesnt-need-to-be-readable-anymore/): Readable code was always a compromise for humans\. Explainable is the new bar\. Yuval and Geoffrey Huntley talk about why Git is already dead, why frontier intelligence plateaued a year ago, and why the next programming languages get built for agents, not people\.
- [The Model Routing Paradigm That Changed My Mind](https://www.ai21.com/yaap/the-model-routing-paradigm-that-changed-my-mind/): Models are cheap\. Routing them well is not\. Yuval and Tomás break down why naive model routing quietly costs you more, and why it’s really a robotics problem in disguise\.
- [Every Learner Gets Their Own Andrew](https://www.ai21.com/yaap/every-learner-gets-their-own-andrew/): Courses are built for everyone\. That means they're built for no one\. Yuval and Ryan unpack how DeepLearning\.ai is turning online education into a conversation — and why your next teacher might never have had a classroom\.
- [Everything But the Model: Harness Engineering](https://www.ai21.com/yaap/everything-but-the-model-harness-engineering/): No harness, no production\. Yuval and Mike break down what harness engineering actually is, why MCP matters, and how to get your agent out of your laptop and into the world\.

